      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T09:06:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Don\u0027t know if you are commenting in my idea ...\n\nNo, not directly on your idea. Sorry I didn\u0027t read it carefully, it is also a valid approach IMHO.\n\nWhat I meant is that we could pass metrics via assisted injection from both http and ssh layers. I didn\u0027t try it but here is what I observe from the source code:\n\n* In the `com.google.gerrit.sshd.commands.Receive` we explicitly create `AsyncReceiveCommits` using its `factory.create` method. At that place we could pass SSH specific metrics implementation as a parameter.\n\n* In the `GitOverHttpServlet.ReceiveFactory` we also create an `AsyncReceiveCommits` and can pass http specific metrics implementation.\n\nBoth ssh and http metric implementations implement an interface defined in the `com.google.gerrit.server.git.receive` package. Therefore, the direction of dependencies is correct.",
      "parentUuid": "db8fa472_3f40b928",
      "revId": "28c7ebb9961552a7414b9dc4897b54f2fdd54f98",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
